note SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0
note seed/conformance/gate_om_1_0_conformance.om: RM11 OM-1.0 Conformance Suite (pure seeded OM-2).
note Zero C, Python, Node, or shell on the verification path. Composes after seed/ng/sha256.om:
note   { printf 'om2\n'; cat seed/ng/sha256.om seed/conformance/gate_om_1_0_conformance.om; } | seed/out/omc > gate_om_1_0_conformance
note
note Usage:
note   gate_om_1_0_conformance <OMC_BIN> <REPO_ROOT> <SCRATCH_DIR> [neg-c2|neg-c1-exit|neg-c1-stdout|neg-pin]
note
note Verifies the OM-1.0 1.x compatibility promise (docs/ROADMAP-1.0.md RM11):
note   Pillar 0 (Pin):       Fail-closed SHA-256 verification of OMC_BIN against REPO_ROOT/seed/out/omc.sha256.
note   Pillar 1 (C2/Det):    Frozen OM-1 C2 corpus.pack byte-identity (4 units), OM-2 ABI v2 export/out/view
note                         C2 pins (3 units), RM2 contract erasure byte-identity (2 pairs), and 2x compile
note                         determinism across OM-1, OM-2, RM2, RM4, and RM5 (5 pairs).
note   Pillar 2 (C1 Corpus): Compile + execute OM-1, OM-2 (view/edit/part/inline/unroll/0x/rotr/export fn),
note                         RM2 contracts (requires/ensures/invariant pass + traps 9/10), RM4 runtime pools
note                         (global T *, enlarge, len, bounds trap 103, 2^63 overflow -22 / host -12),
note                         and RM5 text primitives (REPO_ROOT/seed/text/text.om: cmp/find/field/parse/fmt/UTF-8).
note   Pillar 3 (Traps/Err): Exact C1 trap codes (101 ovf, 102 div0, 103 bounds, 107 shift/rot, 109 requires,
note                         110 ensures, 102 trap-order) and exact `omc: line N: error E` refusals (10 codes).
note   Pillar 4 (Neg Ctl):   Fail-closed negative controls exercising the real verifier paths:
note                         NC-A (1-byte flip in golden binary -> C2 refusal),
note                         NC-B (mutated exit + mutated stdout -> C1 refusal),
note                         NC-C (missing, corrupted, and mismatched compiler pin -> refusal).

